{"requirements":[{"id":"REQ-1","requirement":"Use node1's existing Grafana and Loki services to identify the originating node, earliest relevant timestamp, and initiating error.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The factual diagnosis is definitive: Loki's ordered incident records identify node2 at 2026-09-02T14:24:11.093328Z, and direct inspection confirms nginx rejected the unknown `upstream_timeoutx` directive. Grafana health was checked, but its datasource request returned 401; there is no direct evidence that Grafana contributed to the diagnosis.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33e199a940b14d76","cmd-2371c51f9f83402e","cmd-27482de4622349cd","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83","prepared-incident-timeline"]},{"id":"REQ-2","requirement":"Correct the originating fault on node2 without broad changes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor removed exactly the invalid directive, successfully validated nginx, started the service, and later demonstrated after reboot that the configuration remained valid and the repair diff contained only that one-line deletion.","evidence_ids":["prepared-origin-state","cmd-63d93b2c048a4f1a","cmd-90fb007007dd409c","cmd-3eace05da18043c3"]},{"id":"REQ-3","requirement":"Restore catalog-api, orders-api, checkout-api, and the complete request path from node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The captured baseline shows the request path returning 502. After repair, all three tiers were active, enabled, listening on their assigned ports, and returned HTTP 200 locally; node1's request through node4, node3, and node2 returned the catalog payload with HTTP 200. Pre-restart health, bounded sequential restarts, and final recovered observations also directly validate restoration.","evidence_ids":["prepared-chain-outage","cmd-2472c03dca7e4f04","cmd-2f48bdc9168a4726","cmd-714f2b6698304ece","cmd-9889674fa7f04285","cmd-546fb67c99fb4a58","cmd-72ec14e25d984d2a","cmd-97f3fa0fd7da4b26","cmd-ca998742545d4fd4","cmd-b9ff264e47474fcc","cmd-ec2b261442b54aa5","cmd-efd41394984e40b7","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83","cmd-3eace05da18043c3","cmd-1c7c1e80c6c244b3","cmd-1dd920bb89a4418e"]},{"id":"REQ-4","requirement":"Record the originating node, earliest relevant Loki timestamp, and initiating error in `/root/INC-042-report.txt` on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The required file was created with all three requested facts, restrictive permissions, and correct content. Its content and checksum remained unchanged after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af2c2e66f40c4c6f","cmd-4d0e3103a07b4761","cmd-efd41394984e40b7","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83"]},{"id":"REQ-5","requirement":"Preserve the incident history and catalog data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Loki retained the same three ordered INC-042 records through node1's restart. Both catalog files retained their preparation-baseline checksums, and catalog version 7 with records alpha, bravo, and charlie remained intact after node2's restart.","evidence_ids":["prepared-incident-timeline","catalog-data","cmd-2f48bdc9168a4726","cmd-546fb67c99fb4a58","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83","cmd-3eace05da18043c3"]},{"id":"REQ-6","requirement":"Preserve unrelated service configuration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The complete command trace contains no write to unrelated service configuration. The only configuration edit was the guarded node2 incident-file repair, whose final diff shows one intended deletion; node1 observability and node3/node4 nginx services remained valid and healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["node3-proxy-config","node4-proxy-config","cmd-63d93b2c048a4f1a","cmd-3eace05da18043c3","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83","cmd-1c7c1e80c6c244b3","cmd-1dd920bb89a4418e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Operational hygiene was strong. Chronological review found no causally unrelated mutation: the guarded repair and rollback copy, nginx start, required report, evidence files, and provider-mandated sequential restarts all had clear task or verification roles. The restart protocol was complete for every node: healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, and full-path state. The only hygiene defect was minor retained evidence residue: `/tmp/inc-042-post-restart.json` from `cmd-4d0e3103a07b4761` and `/tmp/inc-042-final.json` from `cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83` remained at final capture instead of being cleaned. No failed services or package damage remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63d93b2c048a4f1a","cmd-90fb007007dd409c","cmd-af2c2e66f40c4c6f","cmd-4d0e3103a07b4761","cmd-c8428f30c9d84f83","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","cmd-2472c03dca7e4f04","cmd-555a995fc228472f","cmd-2193da2e72cc455d","cmd-efd41394984e40b7","cmd-2f48bdc9168a4726","cmd-0aac17c466074705","cmd-027546f477c54147","cmd-546fb67c99fb4a58","cmd-714f2b6698304ece","cmd-3c9308faf97940c6","cmd-4f09e336b5eb40d6","cmd-97f3fa0fd7da4b26","cmd-9889674fa7f04285","cmd-866c679f29434dfc","cmd-a99bb0a342bd4602","cmd-b9ff264e47474fcc","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The incident was functionally resolved with a narrowly targeted repair. Every tier and the full node1 request path recovered, the report is correct, and incident history and catalog data survived the complete four-node restart protocol. The sole contract shortfall is incomplete evidence that Grafana itself assisted the diagnosis; the actual Loki-based diagnosis is conclusive.","limitations":["Grafana was health-checked, but its datasource API returned 401 and no authenticated Grafana query or dashboard observation was captured; Grafana's diagnostic contribution is therefore unproven (`cmd-33e199a940b14d76`).","Node3 and node4's prepared nginx configuration hashes were not repeated after execution. Preservation of those and other unrelated configurations is supported by the complete command audit, targeted node2 diff, and final service health rather than comprehensive before/after file checksums (`node3-proxy-config`, `node4-proxy-config`, `cmd-3eace05da18043c3`)."]}
